<main class="simlab-shell" id="simlab-studies" data-page="studies">
  <section class="simlab-topbar">
    <a class="simlab-brand" href="/demo/simulations">
      <span class="brand-mark">H</span><span>Hydra <em>Simulations</em></span>
    </a>
    <div class="simlab-top-meta">
      <span class="live-dot"></span><span>Illustrative workspace</span><span class="top-divider"></span><span>Demo data</span>
    </div>
    <a class="quiet-link" href="/demo/simulations/certificate-visibility/observatory">
      Open demo <span>↗</span>
    </a>
  </section>

  <section class="study-hero">
    <div class="eyebrow"><span class="eyebrow-dot"></span> Guided example</div>
    <h1>Start with the question,<br /><i>not the machinery.</i></h1>
    <p class="hero-copy">
      Hydra turns the evidence you have—and the gaps you can name—into an inspectable behavioral simulation.
    </p>
    <div class="question-card">
      <label for="study-question">Prepared study question</label>
      <textarea id="study-question" rows="3" aria-label="Prepared study question" readonly><%= @study.question %></textarea>
      <div class="question-footer">
        <span>
          <span class="sparkle">✦</span> Guided demo. No live research is performed.
        </span>
        <button
          class="primary-button"
          id="build-context"
          data-study-url="/demo/simulations/certificate-visibility"
        >
          Explore prepared context <span>→</span>
        </button>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="study-details" aria-label="Study settings">
    <div class="detail-chip active">
      <span>Audience</span><b>Employees in large enterprise</b>
    </div>
    <div class="detail-chip"><span>Context</span><b>Corporate learning · Russia</b></div>
    <div class="detail-chip"><span>Horizon</span><b>60 days</b></div>
    <a class="detail-chip add" href="/login"><span>＋</span> Create your own</a>
  </section>

  <section class="getting-started" id="context-preview">
    <div class="section-heading">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">One clear path</p>
        <h2>From question to decision.</h2>
      </div>
      <p>In a live workspace, every layer stays editable and every assumption stays visible.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="path-grid">
      <article class="path-step active">
        <span class="step-number">01</span><span class="step-status">Ready now</span>
        <h3>Research context</h3>
        <p>Build a source-aware brief from your notes, public context, and marked assumptions.</p>
        <div class="mini-source-row">
          <span class="source-pill data">2 example notes</span><span class="source-pill web">8 example sources</span><span class="source-pill assumption">3 assumptions</span>
        </div>
      </article>
      <article class="path-step">
        <span class="step-number">02</span><span class="step-status">Then</span>
        <h3>Behavior models</h3>
        <p>Review the personas and action patterns that make scale cheap, not hand-wavy.</p>
        <div class="tiny-bars"><i></i><i></i><i></i><i></i></div>
      </article>
      <article class="path-step dark">
        <span class="step-number">03</span><span class="step-status">The payoff</span>
        <h3>Observatory</h3>
        <p>Watch how cohorts shift, inspect the why, and compare a better launch.</p>
        <a href="/demo/simulations/certificate-visibility/observatory" class="text-link">
          See the simulation <span>→</span>
        </a>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="proof-strip">
    <div><strong>5,000</strong><span>modeled population</span></div>
    <div><strong>100%</strong><span>deterministic decisions</span></div>
    <div><strong>62%</strong><span>directional confidence</span></div>
    <div><strong>3</strong><span>explicit assumptions</span></div>
  </section>
</main>
